# uv
# uv.lock is committed — required for reproducible `uv sync --frozen` in Docker builds (SPEC §13 / H-029).

# State / artifacts
.harness/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Worktrees
# .worktrees/ is the harness's own verb-created root (harness/identity.py);
# .claude/worktrees/ is the Claude Code CLI's agent-dispatch root — different
# owner, same hazard. Keep comments on their own lines: git does not treat a
# trailing '#' on a pattern line as a comment.
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# .codex/ and .gemini/ are committed like .claude/ in this committed-mode repo.
# Ignore only genuinely per-machine bits if any appear (e.g. an absolute-path hook config).

# Run artifacts a verb loop stages at the worktree root, because the wrapper
# mounts only the invoking CWD into each verb's container so `/tmp` never
# resolves there (`commands/harness.md`). Untracked each reads as a dirty
# worktree to the close gate; `git add -A` publishes it instead. Not covered by
# `.harness/` above — both land at the root.
#   gate.log   — verify-gate output for `harness review --gate-log` (#259)
#   /design.md — Step 1.5's design_markdown for `review --design-file`
# `design.md` is root-anchored: it is a name worth tracking under docs/ or
# specs/, unlike the distinctive `gate.log`.
gate.log
/design.md
